16 0 obj
<< /A 51 0 R /Alt (Figure containing four grouped bar graphs comparing physiological parameters among three genotypes \(EET8, ICS60, TSH565\) under different water treatments. Panels show photosynthetic rate \(A\), stomatal conductance \(gs\), intrinsic water use efficiency \(WUEi\), and total dry weight. Error bars and statistical significance letters are present for each group.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 35 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 52 0 R /Alt (Bar graph and Venn diagrams compare differentially expressed genes \(DEGs\) between EET8 and TSH565. Bar graph shows upregulated and downregulated DEG counts. Venn diagrams display overlaps for upregulated and downregulated genes.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 36 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 53 0 R /Alt (Panel A shows a bubble plot with gene ontology terms on the y-axis and significance \(negative log10 p-value\) on the x-axis; bubble color gradates from blue to red with shape and size indicating class and count. Panel B is a grouped horizontal bar chart displaying KEGG pathway enrichment for upregulated \(red\) and downregulated \(blue\) genes, with bubble sizes representing gene counts and bar length encoding significance.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 37 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 54 0 R /Alt (Panel A shows two dot plots for gene ontology enrichment with \215response to stress\216 and \215response to stimulus\216 in the biological process category, and \215protein kinase activity\216 and \215unfolded protein binding\216 in the molecular function category. Dot color represents significance \(from green to red\), while size indicates gene count. Panel B presents an expanded dot plot with more enriched gene ontology terms across biological process, cellular component, and molecular function categories, also color-coded by significance and sized by count.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 40 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
20 0 obj
<< /A 55 0 R /Alt (Complex signaling pathway diagram illustrates plant water deficit response, showing interconnected molecular components and gene expression modules. Colored boxes label THS 565 \(green\), EET 8 \(orange\), and common \(gray\) genes. Major pathways include ABA-dependent and ABA-independent signaling, calcium signaling, transcription factors, and stress-responsive gene expression leading to physiological responses such as tolerance, energy metabolism, osmoprotection, antioxidant system, and others. Flow arrows indicate regulation and interactions among receptors, kinases, transporters, and gene modules.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 41 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
21 0 obj
<< /A 56 0 R /Alt (Diagram comparing physiological, biochemical, and molecular plant responses to drought stress in two genotypes: EET 8 \(panel A\) and TSH 565 \(panel B\). Both panels show a labeled plant with pathways indicating signal transduction, antioxidant activity, water deficit sensing, stomatal conductance, gene expression, and water-use efficiency changes under stress, highlighting genotype-specific responses and tolerance mechanisms, with quantitative values for each parameter.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 37 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
